  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a list of `dominoes`, `dominoes[i] = [a, b]` is **equivalent to** `dominoes[j] = [c, d]` exactly when either (`a == c` and `b == d`), or (`a == d` and `b == c`) - that is, one domino can be rotated to be equal to another domino.\n\nOutput *the number of pairs* `(i, j)` *for which* `0 <= i < j < dominoes.length`*, and* `dominoes[i]` *is **equivalent to*** `dominoes[j]`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: dominoes = [[1,2],[2,1],[3,4],[5,6]]\nOutput: 1\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: dominoes = [[1,2],[1,2],[1,1],[1,2],[2,2]]\nOutput: 3\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= dominoes.length <= 4 * 104`\n* `dominoes[i].length == 2`\n* `1 <= dominoes[i][j] <= 9`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
